## Fallback brand colors (when the prospect's site gives no clean read)

Used in Step 2 only if brand discovery fails. Neutral defaults so the doc
still looks intentional. These are YOURS to change — the skill file has no
hardcoded palette.

- `--primary`: <!-- e.g. #1f2933 (near-black slate) -->
- `--primary-deep`: <!-- e.g. #111827 -->
- `--primary-soft`: <!-- e.g. #eef1f4 (~12% tint) -->
- `--accent`: <!-- e.g. #2563eb -->
- `--accent-soft`: <!-- e.g. #e6efff -->

---

## Our accent (the thin co-branding stripe)

The doc is in the *prospect's* brand; your brand shows up only as a thin
accent (Guardrail 6). Give the generator what it needs for that light touch.

- Company name (for the "Prepared by" footer): [Company]
- Wordmark style: <!-- e.g. lowercase, monospace -->
- One accent color if you want it present: <!-- e.g. #ff5c39, or "none —
  stay fully in the prospect's palette" -->

